tests/golden/check/ffi-a-group-head-names-not-locates.hero:33:8: error[machine_locked_path]: `/opt/foo/include/foo.h` names a path, and a header in a group head says what the machine has, not where this machine keeps it — the next machine keeps it elsewhere
  set `CPATH` to the directory holding it, or name a `package` and let `pkg-config` answer; a header beside this file is written relative, as `sub/foo.h`
tests/golden/check/ffi-a-group-head-names-not-locates.hero:36:23: error[unwritable_name]: this library's name holds `/`, which macOS's and Linux's linkers read below each directory they search and not from the root it names, and `/opt/foo/lib/libfoo.a` names a path from a root, where this machine keeps the library rather than what the machine has
  pass `--library <dir>` with the directory holding it, or name a `package` and let `pkg-config` answer; `link` takes the library's **name**, as `link "sqlite3"`
tests/golden/check/ffi-a-group-head-names-not-locates.hero:39:23: error[unwritable_name]: this library's name holds `/`, which macOS's and Linux's linkers read below each directory they search and not from the root it names, and `:/opt/foo/lib/libfoo.a` names a path from a root, where this machine keeps the library rather than what the machine has
  pass `--library <dir>` with the directory holding it, or name a `package` and let `pkg-config` answer; `link` takes the library's **name**, as `link "sqlite3"`
